From a1cd383038bde66c03c8689f48a3fb4cc971988e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:15:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0991 redfin: sampling profiler for one process (p prof), p
 disp, p phase

p prof start NAME|PID [HZ [SECS [DEPTH [WAITHZ]]]] samples the process's threads:
a local timer at HZ cross-calls only the CPUs whose active thread belongs to the
task; the handler records the interrupted user pc/lr (or the kernel pc plus the
user state saved at entry) and a fault-free frame-pointer walk (AT S1E0R + the
physical aperture). WAITHZ adds off-CPU samples from a kernel thread. The buffer
(8 MiB contiguous) is read over /dev/pmem; tools-claude/sweet-prof.py makes the
profile. p disp logs the display power state. p phase NAME flushes the FB,
SCANOUT and GPU stats windows, logs SWEET PHASE: NAME and marks the profile, so
bench stats lines align with gesture phases.
